.TH MALDOCTRACE 1 "November 2026" "maldoctrace 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
maldoctrace \- analyze malicious Office documents by emulating VBA and Excel 4.0 macros
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B maldoctrace inspect
.I file
.br
.B maldoctrace extract
.I file
.B \-\-out
.I dir
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.br
.B maldoctrace analyze
.I file
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B maldoctrace analyze
.I dir
.B \-\-recursive
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B maldoctrace version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B maldoctrace
extracts VBA and Excel 4.0 (XLM) macros from Office documents, deobfuscates
them and emulates them in a fully simulated environment. No process is started,
no network request is made and no COM object is created. The report shows the
commands the document would run, the payloads it would decode or drop and the
indicators it contains, each traced back to the module, procedure and line, or
sheet and cell, that produced it.
.PP
Supported inputs are OLE/CFB (.doc, .xls, .ppt), OOXML (.docx, .docm,
\&.xlsx, .xlsm, .pptm), RTF and plain VBA text. Documents without macros are checked for
remote template injection, external OLE objects, DDE fields, RTF Equation Editor
exploits and VBA stomping.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B inspect
Print an overview of the container: format, streams and macro modules.
.TP
.B extract
Write the decompressed VBA modules to the directory given with
.BR \-\-out .
.B \-\-force
overwrites existing files.
.TP
.B analyze
Extract, deobfuscate and emulate the macros and print a report.
.TP
.B version
Print the version and the JSON report schema version.
.SH ANALYZE OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-format " text|json|jsonl"
Output format (default: text). jsonl prints one JSON object per file.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " duration"
Per-file analysis timeout, for example 30s (default: 2m0s).
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-steps " N"
Interpreter step budget per module (default: 1000000).
.TP
.BI \-\-input\-format " vba"
Treat the input as plain VBA source text.
.TP
.B \-\-show\-strings
In text output, list the reconstructed strings with their locations.
.TP
.BI \-\-dump\-payloads " dir"
Write decoded payloads and dropped files to
.IR dir / sha256 /
with neutral extensions and a manifest.json.
.TP
.BI \-\-password " password"
Extra password to try on encrypted documents, before the built-in list
(Excel's default password VelvetSweatshop and common passwords).
May be repeated.
.TP
.B \-\-pcode
Analyse every module from the VBA code rebuilt from its compiled p\-code
instead of its source. Modules whose source does not match their p\-code
(VBA stomping) are always analysed from the p\-code.
.TP
.BI \-\-fail\-on " level"
Exit with status 3 when the verdict of an analyzed file is at least
.I level
(\fBsuspicious\fR or \fBmalicious\fR). Without it the exit status does not
depend on the verdict.
.TP
.B \-\-recursive
Analyze every file under a directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-workers " N"
Number of files analyzed in parallel in recursive mode (default: 20).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, even when suspicious indicators are found.
.TP
.B 1
Analysis or internal error.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.TP
.B 3
\-\-fail\-on was given and at least one file reached that verdict.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
maldoctrace analyze suspicious.doc
maldoctrace analyze suspicious.xls \-\-format json
maldoctrace analyze sample.docm \-\-dump\-payloads ./out
maldoctrace analyze ./quarantine \-\-recursive \-\-format jsonl
maldoctrace extract suspicious.doc \-\-out ./vba
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR olevba (1)
.PP
https://github.com/debugactiveprocess/MaldocTrace
